# Patch1 has no a/ and b/ prefixes and edits dir/s.c and z.c. Patch2 has git's
# prefixes, renames dir/s.c to dir/t.c with no hunks, and makes the same z.c
# edit, so the run picks -p1, under which z.c pairs and is left out and patch1's
# dir/s.c strips to s.c. The rename's source must strip the same way to match:
# dir/s.c's section must say that the other patch renames the file to dir/t.c,
# and the rename's section must say that the other patch also names dir/s.c with
# text changes.
bin: DIFFOFDIFFS
args: patch1 patch2
exit: 0
